/* cockpit.ini's `indicator` group: the sweep the needle runs through,
   degrees, zero straight up and positive clockwise. -34 is up-and-left
   and +127 is down-and-right, a 161 degree arc through the top -- which
   is exactly the arc the game's own HUD screenshot shows on both gauges
   (opt_cock_all.csi: grey, then gold over the top, then red down the
   right). indicatorShift is the offset from the gauge's own centre that
   the sweep is struck about. */
#define HUD_IND_ANG_MIN  -34.000f   /* indicatorAngMin */
#define HUD_IND_ANG_MAX  127.000f   /* indicatorAngMax */
#define HUD_IND_SHIFT_X   22.000f   /* indicatorShiftX */
#define HUD_IND_SHIFT_Y    0.000f   /* indicatorShiftY */


/* THE DIAL'S OWN GEOMETRY, measured off cockpit_sp1 and cockpit_sp2
   rather than read, because no config file carries it. cockpit_sp1 is the
   dial -- a dark translucent disc, a silver rim and a GOLD tube running
   the whole sweep; cockpit_sp2 is the same ring in two tones, RED over
   the sweep and grey elsewhere. So the port draws sp1 whole as the track
   and reveals a SECTOR of sp2 up to the value: red filling along gold.

   THE MEASUREMENT IS ITS OWN CHECK. sp1's gold spans -39.3..+125.7 deg,
   sp2's red -38.8..+125.0, and cockpit.ini says -34..+127 -- three
   independent statements of one sweep agreeing to four degrees, which is
   the tube's own end-cap rounding. The ini's pair is what the port uses;
   these two are the reason to believe it. Both rings are centred on their
   texture to within 0.006 of its side. */
#define HUD_DIAL_CU   0.50548f   /* cockpit_sp2's fitted centre */
#define HUD_DIAL_CV   0.49279f
#define HUD_DIAL_R0   0.29947f   /* the ring's inner and outer radius, */
#define HUD_DIAL_R1   0.35960f   /* fractions of the texture's side */

/* WHERE THE TWO DIALS SIT, and this is the one block in this file with
   no config key behind it: cockpit.ini carries indicatorShiftX/Y and
   nothing positional, so the dials' screen place is hardcoded in the exe.
   It is MEASURED instead, off the game's own full-HUD screenshot -- the
   cockpit option preview Textures.1/opt_cock_all.csi, a 250x191 render of
   the 800x600 frame, which shows the whole thing: `3rd' top left, the two
   clocks top centre, `Lap 1/6' top right, `100 Boost' bottom left and
   `29 mph' bottom right.

   Three numbers, each the most robust landmark for its axis. The ring's
   outer radius and its centre Y come out of the arc's VERTICAL extent,
   which runs from its topmost point down to its +127 end: 1.602 R, and
   415..562 in the shot. The centre X is the dark disc's own midpoint,
   22..152. race_ui.c derives the quad's side from R and the art's own
   outer radius above, so the two cannot disagree.

   THE SHOT SHOWS BOTH THE DIAL AND THE MAP PANEL ABOUT A TENTH WIDER THAN
   TALL against art that is square in both cases (168x147 and 182x167).
   Something in the original's 2D path is not a uniform scale and what it
   is has not been recovered; sqrt(4/3) = 1.155 fits the dial to 1.5% and
   the map to 6%, which is a guess and is not applied. Both are drawn
   SQUARE. See known-issues.md. */
